constexpr std::string_view kMethod =
    "For every living person and Dread: derive facts from the exported record (features, role, status, claim verb, bond kinds, tier, archetype, presence, faces) and the world (war pressure and threat on the home city, rural food deficit, lunar surges, node intensity at a held key point, living rivals, resting relics, squatted ruins, open mantles, seated tyrants). Every trope whose entry predicate holds is a spoke; weight = boosts × alignment fit × archetype fit × claim fit. The heaviest spoke is the offered hook, ties broken on trope id; the rest are armed. The offered trope's three acts are bound to the hero's own names and each act lists the threads it can exit along with one typed condition and any archetype cut. No draw decides an assignment; the seed only staggers initiative deadlines.";
constexpr std::string_view kLimits =
    "A compiled offer, not a running story: nothing here advances an act, applies a delta, resolves an abandonment or writes to the cast. Completion and abandonment predicates are exported for a later walker. World facts are coarse (a surge anywhere counts for everyone; reach is the home city). Tropes whose entry names features no well computes yet are listed in the ledger as unreachable rather than hidden.";

